Clawblox: serve HTTP/1 only, and update dependencies with published security advisories

Applies to: Clawblox (https://github.com/nacloos/clawblox) at commit 8be90a0, on its own or after the
other twelve; apply all thirteen in the order of the README's table.
Clawblox is MIT-licensed (see worlds/beach/renderer/LICENSE.clawblox); this patch changes a few
lines of its code and is offered under the same MIT terms. Written for AI Beach.

    git apply /path/to/AI-Beach/patches/clawblox-http1-and-crate-bumps.patch
    cargo build --release

Why (a security audit, 11-02): `cargo audit` on the lock found published advisories in crates the
engine is built with. Most sit on paths a running world never takes (it makes no outbound calls and
unpacks no archives), but one was reachable: `axum::serve` hands connections to hyper-util's "auto"
builder, which answers an HTTP/2 prior-knowledge preface whenever hyper-util's http2 feature is
compiled in (other dependencies turn it on), and h2 had a denial-of-service advisory. Anyone who
could reach a world's port directly could use it. Nothing here needs HTTP/2.

What changes:
- New `src/serve_h1.rs`: every server the CLI starts (`run`, the replay server, the external
  runtime, the app browser) serves with hyper's own HTTP/1 connection, websocket upgrades
  included. It has no HTTP/2 code path. (hyper-util's `http1_only()` doesn't do this: its docs say
  it's ignored once upgrades are on, and a test caught exactly that.)
- `hyper` and `hyper-util` become direct dependencies (both already in the lock).
- Semver-compatible updates in Cargo.lock: aws-lc-rs 1.19.0, aws-lc-sys 0.47.0, crossbeam-epoch
  0.9.21, h2 0.4.20, rustls 0.23.46, rustls-webpki 0.103.16, tar 0.4.46, webpki-roots 1.0.11, zstd
  0.13.4, zstd-safe 7.4.0, zstd-sys 2.1.2. Left as they were (not semver-reachable, and on paths a
  world never uses or not built into the `clawblox` binary at all): quick-xml, quinn-proto, rsa, pyo3.

